# Automated QA Suite Selection (Council VERIFY Step)

During the **VERIFY** step of the Subagent Council Loop (`subagent-council-loop.mdc`), the agent must execute the matching automated suite once headless and report `PASS` or `FAIL` in the Changelog under `### QA`. Never claim a fix is complete without QA output.

---

## 1. Suite Selection Matrix

| Change touches | Command (Headless) | Scope & Details |
|---|---|---|
| **Planning, preview, commit, drag, undo, cursor, overlay** | `.\scripts\run_planning_qa_gate.ps1` | SSOT + AOE + full fixtures (`PlanningQaGate.tscn`) + T3 bible mirror. (Default; do **not** run live Tier 3 unless requested). |
| **Core simulation / bridge / broad combat regression** | `.\scripts\run_regression_tests.ps1 -GodotPath "<godot.exe>"` | Determinism, bridge, and sim unit regression. |
| **Both planning & core sim** | Run both commands in order | One run each. |
| **Class factory / skills / passives** | `.\scripts\run_<class>_qa_gate.ps1` + `.\scripts\run_<class>_live_qa.ps1` | Full Knight-bar depth required (`class-qa-standards.mdc`). |
| **Focused swap-only iteration** | `.\scripts\run_swap_planning_acceptance.ps1` | Iterate until green; then run `run_planning_qa_gate.ps1` once before commit. |

*Run QA **once per turn**. Re-run only if the suite fails and you are fixing toward a new pass.*

### Domain Separation
- **Planning / Move Preview fixes:** Run `.\scripts\run_planning_qa_gate.ps1` ONLY. Do **not** run class gates.
- **Class Skill fixes:** Run `.\scripts\run_<class>_qa_gate.ps1` and `.\scripts\run_<class>_live_qa.ps1` for that specific class. Planning QA is **not** a substitute.

---

## 2. Verification Reporting (Changelog)

Under `### QA` in the turn Changelog, record:
- **Suite name(s)** run
- **Result:** `PASS` or `FAIL`
- **Failure lines:** If `FAIL`, paste/summarize `[FAIL]` lines. Fix upstream at the canonical owner (`global-systems-first.mdc` § QA Fix Discipline); never paper over failures with display fallbacks or per-test branches.
- **Commit gate:** Commit per `auto-commit-absolute.mdc` only after QA passes (or after documenting an owner-approved deferral).
